1
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,008
Infuse the root, use it for coughs.

2
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:35,137
Always find the design
hidden in the random.

3
00:01:36,847 --> 00:01:37,973
What do you see?

4
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:42,853
A turtle shell separated into 13 parts.

5
00:01:43,604 --> 00:01:45,480
Nature's design has power.

6
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:48,066
Oh, the great hunter returns

7
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:50,402
-with bunnies.
-For you, <i>Moolsum.</i>

8
00:01:51,903 --> 00:01:53,905
Want to help me clean
some fish I caught this morning?

9
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:56,783
Don't worry about him.

10
00:01:56,867 --> 00:01:57,909
Every hunt counts.

11
00:01:57,993 --> 00:02:00,662
I still think that they should
let me go on a real one.

12
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:04,541
My mom thinks I need to be patient
and keep training.

13
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:07,836
-Sounds like Apto.
-At least he believes in you.

14
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:10,047
-Makes one of us.
-Stop.

15
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:12,132
You're gonna make a great healer someday.

16
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:14,343
-He knows it, so do I.
-Guys!

17
00:02:14,426 --> 00:02:17,387
Guys! Guys! Look!

18
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:18,764
-What?
-This!

19
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:20,515
What is that?

20
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,352
-Hair!
-On your face?

21
00:02:23,435 --> 00:02:24,686
Like an Englishman.

22
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:29,358
Neekani, clan mothers are calling council.

23
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:42,245
The scouts brought news
of the English settlement to the south.

24
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:44,706
The rains washed out their dwellings.

25
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:49,294
Disease hit their camp.
They won't make it through another winter.

26
00:02:49,795 --> 00:02:54,466
It seems they're looking
to the Western Woods to rebuild.

27
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:58,845
We've warned them
of the danger that lies inside it.

28
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:00,055
Yes.

29
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:03,517
What lives in there will feed
on them and become strong enough

30
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,601
to leave the woods.

31
00:03:05,227 --> 00:03:06,895
Our village would be in danger.

32
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:08,480
Seski, what do you propose?

33
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:11,191
We stop them before they can reach it.

34
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:14,027
Times are hard enough
without starting a war with them.

35
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:19,074
Our own food supplies will be low
because they've overhunted.

36
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:22,911
Which is why
we should hunt the Western Wood.

37
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:24,705
Neekani.

38
00:03:24,788 --> 00:03:27,499
If we need food,
we should go where there's prey.

39
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:31,920
If it's too much for the hunters, send me.

40
00:03:32,003 --> 00:03:35,173
No one goes in there.
Not us, not the English.

41
00:03:35,257 --> 00:03:36,383
I know the stories.

42
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:39,136
But have you ever even seen it?

43
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:41,054
-The Kollu?
-I don't need to.

44
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:45,225
For generations, our people have lived
in balance with what lies

45
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,644
in those woods by staying out.

46
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:49,146
We do not feed it.

47
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:51,273
That's how we keep it small.

48
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:54,443
Now close your mouth
and open your ears like the others.

49
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:01,533
What was that?

50
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:05,078
You think you know better
than your elders now?

51
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:10,083
The settlers bring war,
disease, a vengeful god.

52
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:13,003
Neekani, please.

53
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:15,756
We already lost your father to their pox.

54
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:21,928
You need to think of this community first,
because what would we...

55
00:04:24,723 --> 00:04:26,683
What would I do without you?

56
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:50,832
-Neekani.
-What are you doing?

57
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,835
I heard what happened at the council.
Awendela told me.

58
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:55,670
Just go home, Kino.

59
00:04:55,754 --> 00:04:58,173
Hey, please don't tell me you're going
where I think you're going.

60
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:01,176
Aren't you too old
to believe those children's stories?

61
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:04,971
-Okay, but...
-Kino, our village needs meat.

62
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:07,432
You're gonna quarter
and drag a bear back yourself?

63
00:05:07,516 --> 00:05:09,184
You needed my help cleaning fish.

64
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,563
Fine.

65
00:05:14,272 --> 00:05:15,899
-The two of us, then.
-Three.

66
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:18,026
You gotta be kidding me.

67
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:21,613
-You need me. I'm real strong.
-Maneese, go home.

68
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:25,242
I come or I tell.

69
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:29,830
Fine.

70
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,457
Come on, keep up.

71
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:14,291
The Western Wood.

72
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:16,918
Doesn't look so bad.

73
00:06:17,669 --> 00:06:20,881
-Are we really doing this?
-Why? Are you scared of the Kollu?

74
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:23,508
No. Just settlers.

75
00:06:26,887 --> 00:06:28,471
Right. Come on, then.

76
00:06:58,043 --> 00:06:59,210
Probably just birds.

77
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,222
Settler!

78
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:23,693
Guys! Guys!

79
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:28,198
Run!

80
00:08:16,579 --> 00:08:17,580
<i>Kwai.</i>

81
00:08:18,707 --> 00:08:19,708
Oh, yeah.

82
00:08:26,089 --> 00:08:30,051
The turtle sure smiled
on you today, didn't it?

83
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:32,637
How did you do that? Scare them off?

84
00:08:33,555 --> 00:08:35,515
It doesn't like this.

85
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,894
You shouldn't be here.

86
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:43,106
-It's not safe.
-We were just hunting.

87
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:46,860
-Will they come back?
-Most definitely. Yes.

88
00:08:49,154 --> 00:08:50,238
But we'll be safe.

89
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:54,743
Camp is near. Come. I can feed you.

90
00:09:00,165 --> 00:09:03,626
Those things are scared of him.
Just stay close.

91
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:08,757
What turtle?

92
00:09:11,301 --> 00:09:12,302
Come on.

93
00:09:25,732 --> 00:09:28,151
Mitig, what were those things?

94
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,529
Not things.

95
00:09:35,617 --> 00:09:36,618
Thing.

96
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:40,622
So what does it want?

97
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:44,250
To eat, to grow...

98
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:47,837
to survive.

99
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,298
Mostly eat.

100
00:09:52,383 --> 00:09:53,510
What does it eat?

101
00:09:55,345 --> 00:09:57,555
It likes the meat that has
the biggest dreams,

102
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,184
that has the endless fear.

103
00:10:02,936 --> 00:10:03,937
It's real.

104
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:07,649
But we're lucky. The turtle protects us.

105
00:10:10,944 --> 00:10:13,196
-You wanna talk to him?
-Talk to who?

106
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:23,957
Maturin, the great turtle,
had been locked in a cosmic battle

107
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:27,836
<i>against the monster,</i>
<i>long before the Earth even existed.</i>

108
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:36,678
<i>After a terrible struggle, Maturin won,</i>
<i>and he banished that thing to Earth,</i>

109
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:39,305
<i>bound inside a falling star.</i>

110
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,770
<i>It's bindings broke open.</i>

111
00:10:47,564 --> 00:10:51,818
<i>The evil spirit was released</i>
<i>and roamed the woods for a million years.</i>

112
00:10:55,405 --> 00:10:58,491
<i>But the turtle showed me</i>
<i>the cavern where it crashed.</i>

113
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:05,623
<i>That's where I found</i>
<i>the remains of its cage,</i>

114
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:09,043
the only thing that could stop it.

115
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:14,632
Where are the rest of your people?

116
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:26,728
<i>My hunting party was hunted.</i>
<i>One by one.</i>

117
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:28,479
By one.

118
00:11:29,606 --> 00:11:30,607
By one.

119
00:11:32,734 --> 00:11:34,819
<i>It wore the skin of a bull moose.</i>

120
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,947
Fur black as midnight.

121
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:41,701
Antlers of sharpened bone...

122
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,955
pierced the men through their heads.

123
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:49,667
Just like stringing beads.

124
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:55,048
Those yellow eyes.

125
00:12:00,345 --> 00:12:03,640
<i>All I could do was hide.</i>

126
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:09,729
I'm so sorry.

127
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:13,358
I've been holding it in for a long time.
Is there a good place to...

128
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,944
Out that way. Stay near the cedars.

129
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:19,113
I can't protect you beyond there.

130
00:12:50,395 --> 00:12:51,396
Nope.

131
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:26,597
Here my boy. Sit down.

132
00:13:27,557 --> 00:13:29,517
You don't want the meat to get cold.

133
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:41,571
Eat.

134
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:46,326
Eat.

135
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:57,337
Eat up. Eat up.

136
00:13:58,796 --> 00:14:00,048
We need more firewood.

137
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:04,218
Hey, what's wrong?

138
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:08,181
He's killing them.
There's bodies carved in the forest.

139
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:09,891
Was that the...

140
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:11,559
Was that the meat?

141
00:14:12,894 --> 00:14:14,562
We have to leave. We have to go.

142
00:14:18,316 --> 00:14:20,693
-What are you doing?
-The root he was smoking.

143
00:14:20,777 --> 00:14:22,153
-I'm a medicine woman.
-No, you're not.

144
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,988
In training. I'm curious.

145
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,243
What are you doing?

146
00:14:30,787 --> 00:14:32,288
That's mine, not yours.

147
00:14:33,206 --> 00:14:35,875
It's my root. My turtle.

148
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:42,090
-We're gonna leave.
-Where are you going?

149
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,009
Well, you can't go out there.
It'll take you.

150
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:48,221
In the worst way that you could imagine.

151
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:52,183
I can deliver you quicker
than the last ones.

152
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:58,147
Be with your ancestors
while your screams are still echoing--

153
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:00,316
Come on, we gotta go!

154
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:02,735
I got it!

155
00:15:10,201 --> 00:15:11,411
Bring it back!

156
00:15:11,953 --> 00:15:15,706
-Keep going! Just keep running!
-You bring me back my dagger!

157
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:20,503
-Keep going! Just keep running!
-You stupid children!

158
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:24,424
-This way.
-I will kill you for this!

159
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:37,645
You don't understand!

160
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:43,317
It's not a monster! That thing!

161
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:45,695
It's a god!

162
00:15:46,988 --> 00:15:51,659
Gods demand sacrifice! I had no choice!

163
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:54,704
It had to be fed!

164
00:15:56,873 --> 00:15:59,041
I gave you the food of the gods!

165
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:03,754
Please come back! Please!

166
00:16:04,297 --> 00:16:06,382
Don't leave me alone!

167
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,968
It was mine!

168
00:16:10,428 --> 00:16:12,597
It was mine!

169
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,569
Can't have any fear.

170
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:48,799
This is impossible.

171
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,552
It killed them outside of the woods.

172
00:16:57,058 --> 00:16:58,559
We're not safe here anymore.

173
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,979
<i>-Nigwis.</i>
-Neekani?

174
00:17:02,063 --> 00:17:04,524
-We're here!
-How is she in there?

175
00:17:05,191 --> 00:17:06,192
Neekani!

176
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,402
-Mother!
-Stay close.

177
00:17:12,782 --> 00:17:13,783
Neekani!

178
00:17:15,076 --> 00:17:16,077
Neekani!

179
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,669
Mom.

180
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:13,050
I found a new god!

181
00:18:22,018 --> 00:18:24,061
Do you know why we've come here?

182
00:18:30,318 --> 00:18:32,320
It's a wide, open land.

183
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:38,951
A new world with the freedom
to worship the one, true god.

184
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:44,040
And do you know what we do
when we come across

185
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:47,168
a smaller, pitiful faith?

186
00:18:52,006 --> 00:18:56,177
We devour it!

187
00:19:16,489 --> 00:19:17,657
Seski...

188
00:19:19,492 --> 00:19:21,243
Seski...

189
00:19:25,623 --> 00:19:27,541
Come now, Seski.

190
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:31,379
Your beloved husband
waits by the Lord's side.

191
00:19:33,798 --> 00:19:38,511
Not quite as handsome as before,
what with the pox and all.

192
00:20:10,376 --> 00:20:15,172
For this to work, you must have faith.

193
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:19,135
And your faith is...

194
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:23,848
insignificant.

195
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:39,905
Prepare to meet thy God!

196
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:48,748
"The Word became flesh,

197
00:20:48,831 --> 00:20:52,209
and we witnessed the glory
of his Son."

198
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:54,712
"He is mighty."

199
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:59,633
"He is vengeful,
and it is time for you to meet him."

200
00:21:13,022 --> 00:21:15,733
Mom? Mom!

201
00:21:27,161 --> 00:21:28,162
Mom!

202
00:21:28,245 --> 00:21:29,705
Mom, no!

203
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:34,293
Mom!

204
00:21:35,169 --> 00:21:36,170
Mom.

205
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:03,697
Neekani.

206
00:22:05,074 --> 00:22:08,202
Listen to me. You have to stop it.

207
00:22:10,496 --> 00:22:13,332
No, we're going to finish this together.
Me and you.

208
00:22:15,459 --> 00:22:18,045
You... you have to protect our home.

209
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:23,133
I'm not strong enough.

210
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:27,346
-I'm not brave enough.
-You are braver than you think.

211
00:22:37,565 --> 00:22:40,526
Mom! No! Mom!

212
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:43,571
No!

213
00:23:27,114 --> 00:23:31,160
The boundary has shifted,
and we need to stop it.

214
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:34,371
Neekani, we have no choice.

215
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:37,625
We have decided to move the village.

216
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:42,463
This place has been our home
for generations.

217
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:47,051
My mother fought and died to protect it.

218
00:23:47,134 --> 00:23:50,054
In the absence
of knowing what path to take,

219
00:23:50,137 --> 00:23:54,350
we have no choice
but to take the one in front of us.

220
00:23:58,270 --> 00:23:59,813
What if there was another way?

221
00:24:06,028 --> 00:24:07,237
Wanna talk to him?

222
00:25:11,635 --> 00:25:14,138
-What's going on?
-She took the root.

223
00:25:15,472 --> 00:25:17,099
From the man in the Western Wood.

224
00:25:18,350 --> 00:25:21,020
-What did you see?
-He showed me how to save us.

225
00:25:23,022 --> 00:25:24,106
How to cage it.

226
00:25:25,691 --> 00:25:26,984
It's what my mother would have done.

227
00:25:27,901 --> 00:25:29,653
And it's what we have to do now.

228
00:25:32,489 --> 00:25:33,907
What do we need to do?

229
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:40,539
<i>The turtle showed Kino</i>
<i>how to find the cave in the Western Wood,</i>

230
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:43,917
<i>where it had crashed</i>
<i>millions of years ago.</i>

231
00:25:54,386 --> 00:25:56,346
<i>We gathered 13 stones...</i>

232
00:25:58,724 --> 00:26:00,684
<i>the shards of its old bindings...</i>

233
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:04,730
<i>to forge a new cage.</i>

234
00:26:20,704 --> 00:26:24,750
<i>We give it enough room to live,</i>
<i>to sleep, and hunt.</i>

235
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:28,712
<i>It will take the colonists,</i>

236
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:31,715
<i>and more will come to replace them.</i>

237
00:26:34,426 --> 00:26:36,220
<i>We cannot keep the settlers out...</i>

238
00:26:38,097 --> 00:26:39,640
<i>but we can keep it in.</i>

239
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:45,395
<i>And once it is caged,</i>
<i>it will leave us to ours.</i>

240
00:26:51,068 --> 00:26:55,197
<i>This keeping of the posts,</i>
<i>this tending of the cage...</i>

241
00:26:58,408 --> 00:27:00,452
<i>we will ensure these shards,</i>

242
00:27:00,536 --> 00:27:05,082
<i>these pillars, remain in place forever.</i>

